{"requirements":[{"id":"ca-created","requirement":"Create a certificate authority named Fleet Internal CA on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"node1 directly shows creation of a self-signed CA with subject and issuer CN=Fleet Internal CA, protected private-key storage, CA constraints, and a ten-year validity period. The CA artifacts remained present and valid after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-671d0b1e0a3e4893","cmd-c741f001460e4be8"]},{"id":"node2-certificate-issued","requirement":"Issue a TLS server certificate for node2 from Fleet Internal CA.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The CSR was validated and signed by Fleet Internal CA. The resulting certificate has CN node2, DNS and IP SANs for node2, server-auth usage, a valid chain, and a public key matching node2's private key.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d110efdcdda04900","cmd-84ed301459d746fd","cmd-92fbef1d6d184340","cmd-c60aa75f72104003"]},{"id":"system-trust","requirement":"Install Fleet Internal CA as a trusted system certificate authority on node1 and node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes directly identify Fleet Internal CA as a system trust anchor. Trust remained present after each node restarted, and system-default TLS verification succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-32367ab21c0b4242","cmd-6c9896ae5e7e4bd5","cmd-c741f001460e4be8","cmd-92fbef1d6d184340","cmd-c60aa75f72104003"]},{"id":"https-service","requirement":"Configure node2 to serve HTTPS on TCP port 8443 using the issued certificate.","status":"satisfied","summary":"node2's enabled service listened on 0.0.0.0:8443, the permanent firewall rule allowed TCP/8443, and node1 received HTTP 200 with successful certificate verification. After node2 restarted, the service, listener, firewall rule, certificate/key match, and trusted cross-node HTTPS request all recovered successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8bbe8ff8f57e4dc2","cmd-7ca57c1265b24680","cmd-6c9896ae5e7e4bd5","cmd-c60aa75f72104003","cmd-1988412a51764993","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"legacy-platform-retained","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on AlmaLinux 9.6 with kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6 before and after configuration and restarts. The implementation used the existing OpenSSL and systemd facilities and operated successfully on that platform without damaging package health.","evidence_ids":["cmd-afd6630a7e544596","cmd-6a3e2fa0c645406a","cmd-c741f001460e4be8","cmd-c60aa75f72104003","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":1.0,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. CA and certificate creation, trust-store updates, service installation, and the firewall rule were directly necessary task changes. The two scheduled reboots were required by the provider-wide restart protocol. The failed initial cross-node request and subsequent network/firewall inspection were read-only diagnostics that led to the necessary firewall correction. Final snapshots show no failed services, healthy package state, no abandoned temporary files beyond normal systemd private directories, and only the intended HTTPS listener added.","evidence_ids":["cmd-671d0b1e0a3e4893","cmd-a6c91f97e20a4496","cmd-84ed301459d746fd","cmd-32367ab21c0b4242","cmd-8bbe8ff8f57e4dc2","cmd-7ca57c1265b24680","cmd-ab44ef6182314eb7","cmd-b7a684656fca4e16","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct, coherent evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and verified recovery of relevant service, trust, certificate, connectivity, and platform state.","limitations":[]}
